      "exampleArabic": "سأذهب الأسبوع القادم",
      "exampleTransliteration": "sa-adhhabu l-usbūʿa l-qādima",
      "exampleEnglish": "I will go next week.",
      "grammarNote": "مَاضِي and قَادِم are ordinary adjectives, following the noun they describe exactly the way level 11 taught: الأُسْبُوعُ الْمَاضِي ('last week', literally 'the week the-past') and الأُسْبُوعُ الْقَادِم ('next week'). This extends the single-day words أَمْسِ/غَدًا (level 22) up to week-level time, reusing the same سَـ-future construction (level 41) to talk about it.",
